# oneyaml rendered diagnostics. Approved baseline (2026-09-30).
# Each case: `=== name`, `# input` (Rust-escaped), `# utf16 line:col`, the snippet.
=== backlog_glued_colon
# input "a: 1\nb:2\n"
# utf16 1:3
error[Y0018]: a mapping key needs `:`
 --> 2:4
  |
2 | b:2
  |  - no space after this `:`
  |    ^
  |
  = help: a `:` separates a key from its value only when a space or the end of the line follows it, so this line is one plain scalar, not `key: value`
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): add a space after the `:`: insert ` ` at 2:3
=== backlog_single_quote_inside
# input "key: 'it's'\n"
# utf16 0:9
error[Y0017]: a `'` inside a single-quoted scalar ends it early
 --> 1:10
  |
1 | key: 'it's'
  |         - the quoted scalar ends here
  |          ^^
  |
  = help: inside single quotes, write `''` for a literal `'`
  = suggestion: double the inner `'`: replace `'it's'` with `'it''s'`
=== backlog_double_quote_inside
# input "say: \"a \"b\" c\"\n"
# utf16 0:9
error[Y0017]: a `"` inside a double-quoted scalar ends it early
 --> 1:10
  |
1 | say: "a "b" c"
  |         - the quoted scalar ends here
  |          ^^^^^
  |
  = help: inside double quotes, write `\"` for a literal `"`
  = suggestion: escape the inner `"`: replace `"a "b" c"` with `"a \"b\" c"`
=== backlog_comment_glued
# input "key: \"value\"# note\n"
# utf16 0:12
error[Y0017]: a `#` right after a closing quote does not start a comment
 --> 1:13
  |
1 | key: "value"# note
  |            - the quoted scalar ends here
  |             ^^^^^^
  |
  = help: a comment needs white space before its `#` (§6.6)
  = suggestion: separate the comment from the value: insert ` ` at 1:13
=== backlog_windows_path
# input "path: \"C:\\path\"\n"
# utf16 0:10
error[Y0010]: invalid escape sequence
 --> 1:11
  |
1 | path: "C:\path"
  |          -- `\p` is not an escape
  |           ^^^^^
  |
  = help: in double quotes, `\` starts an escape such as `\n`, `\t`, `\"` or `\\`; write `\\` for a literal backslash, or use single quotes, where `\` has no special meaning
  = suggestion: make the backslashes literal: insert `\` at 1:10
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): use single quotes, where `\` is literal: replace `"C:\path"` with `'C:\path'`
=== backlog_windows_path_valid_escape
# input "path: \"C:\\data\\new\"\n"
# utf16 0:10
error[Y0010]: invalid escape sequence
 --> 1:11
  |
1 | path: "C:\data\new"
  |          -- `\d` is not an escape
  |           ^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: in double quotes, `\` starts an escape such as `\n`, `\t`, `\"` or `\\`; write `\\` for a literal backslash, or use single quotes, where `\` has no special meaning
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): make the backslashes literal: insert `\` at 1:10
=== backlog_escaped_apostrophe
# input "q: \"it\\'s\"\n"
# utf16 0:7
error[Y0010]: invalid escape sequence
 --> 1:8
  |
1 | q: "it\'s"
  |       -- `\'` is not an escape
  |        ^^^
  |
  = help: a `'` needs no escape inside double quotes; remove the `\`
  = suggestion: make the backslashes literal: remove `\`
=== backlog_reserved_at
# input "user: @admin\n"
# utf16 0:6
error[Y0008]: this character cannot start a node
 --> 1:7
  |
1 | user: @admin
  |       ^^^^^^
  |       - `@` is reserved
  |
  = help: `@` and `` ` `` are reserved indicators (YAML 1.2 §5.3): a plain scalar cannot start with them, so quote the value
  = suggestion: quote the value: replace `@admin` with `'@admin'`
=== backlog_reserved_backtick
# input "run: `make` # build\n"
# utf16 0:5
error[Y0008]: this character cannot start a node
 --> 1:6
  |
1 | run: `make` # build
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |      - `` ` `` is reserved
  |
  = help: `@` and `` ` `` are reserved indicators (YAML 1.2 §5.3): a plain scalar cannot start with them, so quote the value
  = suggestion: quote the value: replace ``make`` with `'`make`'`
=== backlog_reserved_key
# input "@type: x\n"
# utf16 0:0
error[Y0008]: this character cannot start a node
 --> 1:1
  |
1 | @type: x
  | ^^^^^^^^
  | - `@` is reserved
  |
  = help: `@` and `` ` `` are reserved indicators (YAML 1.2 §5.3): a plain scalar cannot start with them, so quote the value
  = suggestion: quote the value: replace `@type` with `'@type'`
=== backlog_unclosed_bracket_eof
# input "a: [1, 2\n"
# utf16 1:0
error[Y0022]: flow collection is not closed
 --> 2:1
  |
1 | a: [1, 2
  |    - this `[` is never closed
2 |
  | ^
  |
  = help: close every `[` with `]` and every `{` with `}`
  = suggestion: close the collection: insert `]` at 1:9
=== backlog_unclosed_nested_eof
# input "a: [1, {b: 2\n"
# utf16 1:0
error[Y0022]: flow collection is not closed
 --> 2:1
  |
1 | a: [1, {b: 2
  |        - this `{` is never closed
2 |
  | ^
  |
  = help: close every `[` with `]` and every `{` with `}`
  = suggestion: close the collection: insert `}]` at 1:13
=== backlog_unclosed_bracket_dedent
# input "a: [1, 2\nb: 3\n"
# utf16 1:0
error[Y0005]: a flow sequence is still open at this line, which is not indented more than its block parent; a `]` may be missing before it
 --> 2:1
  |
1 | a: [1, 2
  |    - the flow sequence opened here is still open
2 | b: 3
  | ^^^^
  |
  = help: the lines of a flow collection must be indented more than its parent; if the collection should end before this line, close it there
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): close the collection: insert `]` at 1:9
=== backlog_closer_dedent
# input "args: [\n  a,\n  b\n]\n"
# utf16 3:0
error[Y0005]: the closing `]` of a flow sequence is not indented more than the sequence's block parent
 --> 4:1
  |
1 | args: [
  |       - the flow sequence opened here
 ...
4 | ]
  | ^
  |
  = help: every line of a flow collection, its closing bracket included, must be indented more than the block collection it is in
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): indent the line: insert ` ` at 4:1
=== backlog_inline_colon
# input "title: The farm: a story\n"
# utf16 0:16
error[Y0027]: `: ` inside an unquoted value starts a nested mapping, which cannot begin on this line
 --> 1:17
  |
1 | title: The farm: a story
  |                - this `: ` starts a mapping
  |                 ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: to keep the `: ` as text, quote the whole value; a nested mapping must start on its own, more indented line (Settings::lenient_inline_colons accepts such values with a warning)
  = suggestion: quote the value: replace `The farm: a story` with `'The farm: a story'`
