=== backlog_tab_indent
# input "a:\n\t- b\n"
# utf16 1:1
error[Y0016]: tabs cannot be used for block indentation
 --> 2:2
  |
2 |     - b
  |     ^^^
  |
  = help: YAML indents with spaces only; replace the tabs used for indentation here with spaces
=== backlog_unterminated_quote
# input "a: \"abc\nb: 1\n"
# utf16 1:0
error[Y0011]: a double-quoted scalar is still open at a line that is not indented more than its parent; a closing `"` may be missing
 --> 2:1
  |
1 | a: "abc
  |    - the quoted scalar starts here
2 | b: 1
  | ^
  |
  = help: a quoted scalar goes on until its closing quote, and its continuation lines must be indented more than its parent; if it should end on its first line, add the closing quote there
  = suggestion (may be incorrect): close the quote on this line: insert `"` at 1:8
=== range_schema_duplicate_key
# input "a: 1\nb: 2\nc: 3\na: 4\n"
# utf16 3:0
error[Y1013]: duplicate key `a`
 --> 4:1
  |
1 | a: 1
  | - first defined here
 ...
4 | a: 4
  | ^
  |
  = help: remove one of the entries, or use DuplicateKeys::LastWins (Compat::serde_yaml()) to keep the last value
=== range_schema_warning
# input "%YAML 1.1\n---\na: yes\n"
# utf16 0:9
warning[Y1000]: %YAML 1.1 document parsed as YAML 1.2
 --> 1:10
  |
1 | %YAML 1.1
  |          ^
=== range_limits_depth
# input "a:\n  b:\n    c: 1\n"
# utf16 2:4
error[Y2000]: collections are nested too deeply
 --> 3:5
  |
3 |     c: 1
  |     ^^^^
  |
  = help: raise Limits::max_depth (currently 2)
=== range_serde_path
# input "ports:\n  - port: 80\n  - port: 99999\n"
# utf16 2:10
error[Y3001]: integer 99999 is out of range for u16
 --> 3:11
  |
3 |   - port: 99999
  |           ^^^^^
  |
  = path: ports[1].port
